{"id":"bp01","name":"Balanced Brackets","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["text"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A configuration parser must check the brackets of an expression before evaluating it. You are given a string <code>text</code> that can contain any characters.</p>\n<p>The brackets are <code>[]</code>, <code>{}</code> and <code>()</code>. All other characters are ignored. The brackets are <b>balanced</b> if every opening bracket is closed by a bracket of the same type, in the correct order: a bracket opened inside another one must be closed before it.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return <code>true</code> if the brackets of <code>text</code> are balanced, and <code>false</code> otherwise. A string with no brackets is balanced.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>text = \"{ cfg[(a + b) * c] }\"</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">true</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> string text<br><b>[output]</b> boolean</div>","starter":"def solution(text):\n    # write your code here\n    return True\n","hints":["Une pile : on empile chaque ouvrant, et chaque fermant doit correspondre au sommet de la pile.","À la fin, la pile doit être vide (sinon un ouvrant n'a jamais été fermé)."],"summary_fr":"Dire si les crochets [], accolades {} et parenthèses () du texte sont bien appariés et bien imbriqués. Les autres caractères sont ignorés.","tags":["pile (stack)","dict","cas limites"],"minutes":12,"source":"exercism/problem-specifications (MIT) · matching-brackets","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"text":"{ cfg[(a + b) * c] }"},"expected":{"value":true}},{"input":{"text":"f(x[0)]"},"expected":{"value":false}}],"hidden_n":24,"hidden":"","solution":""}